			"3": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "KUWAHARA\n\nThe Kuwahara filter was originally developed to remove noise from an image. \nIt wasn't particularly good at removing noise, but it had artistic potential.\nThe filter can be used to make an image look like an oil painting.\nTherefore this filter works best on figurative content\n\nDo take care when increasing the radius!\nThe more you increase it, the more GPU power it will consume."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 194.411895751953125,
					"width": 449.030670166015625,
					"x": 407.33770751953125,
					"y": -103.4069366455078125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"46": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "KUWAHARA\nEXAMPLE: CARTOON DRAWING\n\nIn this example we're taking the test card and give it a cartoon look by using the Kuwahara filter\nTo achieve this, we're using the filter to get an oily image which we send to the bottom layer of the video mixer.\nNext, we take the filter's output again to get an edge out of it and layer that on top of the oily image."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 602.82208251953125,
					"width": 1407.6260986328125,
					"x": 405.9725341796875,
